// PostApiTopologyWithBodyWithResponse Returns the service topology with RED statistics on services and connections
//
// Returns the service topology for a time range: one node per
// `service.namespace` + `service.name` pair, and one edge per observed
// direction of calls between two nodes. Nodes and edges each carry the
// RED statistics selected via `nodeStatistics` and `edgeStatistics`.
//
// Edges join to nodes by service identity, not by an opaque id. Peers
// that never reported telemetry of their own — databases, brokers,
// third-party APIs — appear as `inferred` nodes without statistics, so
// the graph stays whole.
//
// Not paginated, and the grouping is not client-selectable; see
// `GetTopologyRequest`. Edge statistics come from a different metric
// than node statistics and are not comparable to them; see
// `TopologyEdgeStatistics`.
